IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aca-dates`
IMPORT `aca-amounts`
IMPORT `aca-weekly`

-- Accident Compensation Act 1985 (Vic) -- worked cases for the weekly payments and non-economic loss questions
-- (aca-weekly.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (and, for the indexed ceilings and the
-- over-70% figures, from Gazette S 363 of 30 June 2026); none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a
-- claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `s 91E -- the kind of claim`

-- Injured and claimed in 1996, entitled at 12 November 1997: a pre-12 November 1997 claimant.
#ASSERT `What kind of weekly payments claim is mine` (`d` 1 3 1996) (`d` 1 4 1996) TRUE EQUALS JUST `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant`
-- The same claim, but not entitled at that date: no kind of claim the sections rate.
#ASSERT `What kind of weekly payments claim is mine` (`d` 1 3 1996) (`d` 1 4 1996) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The last day before 12 November 1997, and the day itself.
#ASSERT `What kind of weekly payments claim is mine` (`d` 1 11 1997) (`d` 11 11 1997) TRUE EQUALS JUST `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant`
#ASSERT `What kind of weekly payments claim is mine` (`d` 1 11 1997) (`d` 12 11 1997) TRUE EQUALS JUST `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010`
-- 4 April and 5 April 2010.
#ASSERT `What kind of weekly payments claim is mine` (`d` 1 3 2010) (`d` 4 4 2010) FALSE EQUALS JUST `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010`
#ASSERT `What kind of weekly payments claim is mine` (`d` 1 3 2010) (`d` 5 4 2010) FALSE EQUALS JUST `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010`

§§ `s 91E -- the entitlement periods`

-- A claim from 2012: 13 weeks, then 117.
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 1 2 2012) 13 EQUALS `the first entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 1 2 2012) 14 EQUALS `the second entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 1 2 2012) 130 EQUALS `the second entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 1 2 2012) 131 EQUALS `after the second entitlement period`
-- Received on 31 December 2004: 91 weeks; on 1 January 2005: 117 weeks.
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` (`d` 31 12 2004) 104 EQUALS `the second entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` (`d` 31 12 2004) 105 EQUALS `after the second entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` (`d` 1 1 2005) 105 EQUALS `the second entitlement period`
-- A pre-12 November 1997 claimant: 26 weeks, then 78.
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` (`d` 1 4 1996) 26 EQUALS `the first entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` (`d` 1 4 1996) 27 EQUALS `the second entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` (`d` 1 4 1996) 104 EQUALS `the second entitlement period`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period am I in` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` (`d` 1 4 1996) 105 EQUALS `after the second entitlement period`

§§ `s 93C(1) -- after the second entitlement period`

-- Second period expired 30 March 2024, assessed with no capacity indefinitely: (a) applies.
#ASSERT `Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 30 3 2024) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Expired on 31 March 2024: (a) alone is not enough ...
#ASSERT `Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 31 3 2024) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ... the (c) determination (more than 20% impairment) is.
#ASSERT `Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 31 3 2024) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A pre-12 November 1997 claimant with a serious injury: (b).
#ASSERT `Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Serious injury counts only for a pre-1997 claimant.
#ASSERT `Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period` `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An approved s 93CD application.
#ASSERT `Do my weekly payments go on after the second entitlement period` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` (`d` 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 93A, 93B, 93C(2), 93CD(5) -- the weekly payment`

-- Arguments: claim, period, PIAWE, current weekly earnings, current work capacity, deductible amount, serious injury,
-- s 93C(1) applies, s 93CD approved, a day in the week.
-- First period, 2010+ claim, no capacity: 95% of $2,000 = $1,900, under the $3,000 ceiling (2026-27).
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 2000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1900
-- 95% of $4,000 = $3,800: capped at $3,000; on 30 June 2026 the 2025-26 cap of $2,930; on 1 July 2026 $3,000.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 4000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 4000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST 2930
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 4000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST 3000
-- With capacity, earning $500, deductible $100: $1,900 - $100 - $500 = $1,300 (against $3,000 - $500 = $2,500).
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 2000 500 TRUE 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1300
-- Second period, capacity, $500 earned: 80% of $2,000 less 80% of $500 = $1,600 - $400 = $1,200.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the second entitlement period` 2000 500 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1200
-- Second period, no capacity, $4,000 PIAWE, a 2025-26 week: 80% = $3,200, capped at $2,930.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the second entitlement period` 4000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST 2930
-- Pre-1997 claimant with a serious injury, earning $500: 90% x $2,000 - 90% x $500 = $1,350, against $1,740 - $450 =
-- $1,290: $1,290. s 93B(1)(a) applies with a current work capacity too (NOTES.md finding 4).
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` `the second entitlement period` 2000 500 TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1290
-- Pre-1997 claimant without a serious injury, no capacity: 80% of $2,000 = $1,600 (under $1,740).
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` `the second entitlement period` 2000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1600
-- 1997-2010 claim, first period, $2,400 PIAWE: 95% = $2,280, capped at $2,200 (2026-27) or $2,150 (2025-26).
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 2400 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 2200
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 12 November 1997 and before 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 2400 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST 2150
-- After the second period under s 93C(1): 80% of $2,000 = $1,600.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `after the second entitlement period` 2000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1600
-- After the second period under s 93CD(5), earning $600: $1,600 - $480 = $1,120.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `after the second entitlement period` 2000 600 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1120
-- Neither: the entitlement has ceased.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `after the second entitlement period` 2000 600 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 0
-- A pre-1997 serious injury continuing only through s 93CD is paid at 80%: $1,600 - $400 = $1,200 (not $1,290).
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` `after the second entitlement period` 2000 500 TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1200
-- ... and through s 93C(1)(b) at 90%: $1,290.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim by a pre-12 November 1997 claimant` `after the second entitlement period` 2000 500 TRUE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 1290
-- Earnings above the rate: $950 - $1,200 is below nothing: no payment.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 1000 1200 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 0
-- A week in 2027-28: the ceiling is not deposited.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `a claim first made on or after 5 April 2010` `the first entitlement period` 2000 0 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 93CD -- keeping weekly payments while working`

-- Arguments: injury, decision day, hours, earnings, incapable of more, second period expiry, whole person impairment.
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2026) 15 257 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2026) 15 256 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2026) 14 300 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2026) 15 300 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Expiry on 31 March 2024: more than 20% needed; 20% is not more than 20%.
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2026) 20 300 TRUE (`d` 31 3 2024) 20 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2026) 20 300 TRUE (`d` 31 3 2024) 21 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2025-26: $251.
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2025) 15 251 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2025) 15 250 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An injury before 5 April 2010 (earlier s 93CD), and a decision in 2027-28 (amount not deposited).
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 4 4 2010) (`d` 1 8 2026) 15 300 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can my s 93CD application be approved` (`d` 1 6 2012) (`d` 1 8 2027) 15 300 TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 93CD(3): 28 days from 10 December 2026 is 7 January 2027 (plain days).
#ASSERT `By when must my s 93CD application be decided` (`d` 10 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 7 1 2027

§§ `ss 93E, 93F -- age`

-- Retirement age reached 1 January 2016; 130 weeks (910 days) before is 5 July 2013.
-- Injured 5 July 2013: s 93E, 130 weeks at most.
#ASSERT `Does my age stop my weekly payments` (`d` 5 7 2013) (`d` 1 1 2016) (`d` 1 8 2026) 130 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my age stop my weekly payments` (`d` 5 7 2013) (`d` 1 1 2016) (`d` 1 8 2026) 131 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Injured 4 July 2013: not s 93E; s 93F stops payments from retirement age.
#ASSERT `Does my age stop my weekly payments` (`d` 4 7 2013) (`d` 1 1 2016) (`d` 31 12 2015) 200 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my age stop my weekly payments` (`d` 4 7 2013) (`d` 1 1 2016) (`d` 1 1 2016) 200 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 93EA claimed: not encoded.
#ASSERT `Does my age stop my weekly payments` (`d` 4 7 2013) (`d` 1 1 2016) (`d` 1 8 2026) 200 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 93CE -- superannuation`

-- Week 53, $1,000 weekly payment, 12%: $120.
#ASSERT `How much superannuation must be paid for me this week` (`d` 1 6 2012) 53 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1000 12 EQUALS JUST 120
-- Week 52: not yet.
#ASSERT `How much superannuation must be paid for me this week` (`d` 1 6 2012) 52 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1000 12 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Retirement age, extra employer contributions, no nomination: none.
#ASSERT `How much superannuation must be paid for me this week` (`d` 1 6 2012) 60 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 12 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much superannuation must be paid for me this week` (`d` 1 6 2012) 60 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 1000 12 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much superannuation must be paid for me this week` (`d` 1 6 2012) 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 12 EQUALS JUST 0
-- An injury before 5 April 2010.
#ASSERT `How much superannuation must be paid for me this week` (`d` 4 4 2010) 60 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 1000 12 EQUALS NOTHING

