§§ `s 98C -- the formula amounts`

-- Arguments: kind, degree, Chapter 3 impairment, spinal, injury, calculation day.
-- Injured 1 March 2014, calculated 1 August 2026.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 9 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 10 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 18810
-- $18,810 + 10 x $2,830 = $47,110.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 20 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 47110
-- 30%: $18,810 + 20 x $2,830 = $75,410; 31%: $75,260 + $4,700 = $79,960; 70%: $75,260 + 40 x $4,700 = $263,260.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 30 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 75410
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 31 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 79960
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 70 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 263260
-- Over 70%, at the calculation date (2026-27): 71% $369,510 + $41,360 = $410,870; 75% $369,510 + 5 x $41,360 = $576,310;
-- 80% $783,110, capped at $783,000; 81% $783,000.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 71 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 410870
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 75 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 576310
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 80 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 783000
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 81 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 783000
-- 2025-26: 71% $358,420 + $40,120 = $398,540. 2027-28: not deposited.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 71 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2025) EQUALS JUST 398540
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 71 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Under 70% the relevant date is the injury: a 2027-28 calculation still answers.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 40 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST 122260

-- The modified ratings. 10% including a Chapter 3 (non-spinal) 5%: (c)(i) $18,810 beats (b)(i) at 10.00 ($11,670).
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 10 5 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 18810
-- 5% Chapter 3 alone: degree 5 gives 0; modified 10.00 gives $11,670.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 5 5 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 11670
-- 9% spinal: modified 10.80, (b)(ii): ($11,670 + 0.8 x $9,940) x 1.1 = $19,622 x 1.1 = $21,584.20.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 9 9 TRUE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 21584.2
-- 10% spinal: modified 11.00, (c)(ii): ($18,810 + $2,830) x 1.1 = $23,804 (below $75,410).
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 10 10 TRUE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 23804
-- 25% spinal: modified 25.25: ($18,810 + 15.25 x $2,830) x 1.1 = $61,967.50 x 1.1 = $68,164.25.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 25 25 TRUE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 68164.25
-- 29% spinal: modified 29.05 gives $79,993.65, above the (c)(ii)(B) cap of $75,410: $75,410.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 29 29 TRUE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 75410
-- 25% spinal for an injury on 1 March 2003 (before 3 December 2003): the (c) amount then in force is not deposited.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 25 25 TRUE (`d` 1 3 2003) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Injured 1 March 2008: (2)(d) as printed ($122,260); (2)(c) the amount then in force (not deposited).
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 40 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2008) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 122260
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 20 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2008) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 40 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2003) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Psychiatric: 29% nil; 30% $75,410; 31% $79,960; 71% (2026-27) $410,870.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent psychiatric impairment` 29 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent psychiatric impairment` 30 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 75410
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent psychiatric impairment` 31 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 79960
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent psychiatric impairment` 71 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 410870
-- A foetus: $67,660. An injury on 1 July 2014: not this Act.
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `the loss of a foetus` 0 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 67660
#ASSERT `What do the s 98C formulas give for my non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 40 0 FALSE (`d` 1 7 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 98C(11) -- the lump sum`

-- 75% injured 1 March 2014: the formulas give $576,310; the maximum at the injury date is $555,350.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 75 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 555350
-- 81%: $783,000 cut to $555,350 (NOTES.md finding 9).
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 81 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 555350
-- 71%: $410,870 is below it.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 71 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2014) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 410870
-- Injured 1 March 2013, 75%: the maximum then in force is not deposited.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 75 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2013) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Injured 1 March 2013, 40%: $122,260.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 40 0 FALSE (`d` 1 3 2013) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 122260
-- 1 July 2013, the first day of the year the printed maximum is read for: 81% gives $555,350.
#ASSERT `How much is my lump sum for non-economic loss` `permanent impairment other than psychiatric` 81 0 FALSE (`d` 1 7 2013) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST 555350
